# SafetyXAcademy Company DNA

Before any brand-facing work (brand naming, visual identity, design, copy, email, SEO, UI, or marketing assets), read and follow the repository root file:

`COMPANY-DNA.md`

That file is the permanent source of truth. Do not invent brand spellings or redesign the identity without explicit owner instruction.

## Brand architecture (three approved forms)

| Role | Form |
|------|------|
| Official written identity | `SafetyXAcademy` |
| Full visual identity | `safetyXacademy` (X in Safety Orange) |
| Compact visual identity | `SXA` (official monogram) |

These are complementary assets, not competing names. No fourth spelling or logo variation without explicit approval.

## Quick locks

| Rule | Value |
|------|--------|
| Written brand name | `SafetyXAcademy` |
| Visual wordmark | `safetyXacademy` (`X` in Safety Orange) |
| Official monogram | `SXA` |
| Safety Orange | `#FF6600` (use existing design token if present) |
| SEO title suffix | `\| SafetyXAcademy` |
| Email sender | `SafetyXAcademy <info@safetyxacademy.nl>` |
| Domain | `safetyxacademy.nl` |

## Usage decision (short)

- Plain text / SEO / schema / email subject / legal / documents → `SafetyXAcademy`
- Prominent visual space with enough horizontal room → `safetyXacademy` (orange X)
- Small square / circular / favicon / Google icon / email logo / app icon → `SXA`

## Agent behaviour

1. Preserve `SafetyXAcademy` in prose, SEO, schema, email, legal, and forms.
2. Preserve `safetyXacademy` where a styled full wordmark is appropriate; only the X is orange.
3. Preserve `SXA` as the official compact monogram in approved small contexts; do **not** flag it as inconsistent branding.
4. Never use variants such as `Safety X Academy`, `SafetyXacademy`, or `safetyxacademy` as the written brand name.
5. Do not invent additional abbreviations or logo treatments; do not replace existing approved SXA icons automatically.
6. Do not globally replace brand names or redesign working components unless explicitly asked.
7. If existing code or copy conflicts with `COMPANY-DNA.md`, flag the inconsistency — do not silently “fix” the brand to match old pages.
8. If uncertain which version to use, follow the Usage decision rule in `COMPANY-DNA.md`.
9. Only update `COMPANY-DNA.md` when the owner explicitly instructs a DNA change.
